WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.792
Raj: Forty queued builds are waiting now. Twelve earlier attempts failed fetching dependencies.

2
00:00:06.792 --> 00:00:13.729
Priya: Okay, that's our blast radius currently. Just to confirm, no production deployments?

3
00:00:13.729 --> 00:00:20.593
Lukas: Check deployment receipts, not dashboard colors. A failed run might complete side effects.

4
00:00:20.593 --> 00:00:27.194
Anika: The pipeline's red before deployment here. Receipts show no deploy requests, right?

5
00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:34.202
Hannah: Correct for these twelve failed attempts. I'll also check partial artifact uploads.

6
00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:40.418
Raj: I'm on it for queue snapshots. Duplicate manual retries are held separately.

7
00:00:40.418 --> 00:00:47.475
Lukas: Keep original run identifiers with attempts. Otherwise we'll lose the deduplication boundary.

8
00:00:47.475 --> 00:00:54.075
Priya: So, hold new dispatch for now. Developers can still submit reviewed changes.

9
00:00:54.075 --> 00:01:00.988
Hannah: I'll keep an eye on uploads. Any incomplete object stays outside release selection.

10
00:01:00.988 --> 00:01:07.900
Anika: Fair, submissions aren't deployments or retries. I'll make that distinction quite clear.

